# [Fix] [MI355X] qwen38_flash_next: Keep the draft's graph captures out of SGLang's capture check
# sgl-project/sgl-amd-mono PR: https://github.com/sgl-project/sgl-amd-mono/pull/204  (commit a88e568 on sgl-amd-mono main 7a5a075)
# Patch for the image's sgl-amd-mono checkout (/sgl-workspace/sgl-amd-mono, 32a12203), not SGLang; the source file
# only (the unit test of the PR dropped). Since sgl-project/sglang#46210 the draft CUDA graph runners run the
# capture tail hooks, and SGLang's monokernel capture check rejects the MTP draft's decode step, so c1-c8
# (--enable-amd-monokernel) fail at the draft decode capture. No SGLang change is needed: the draft's build makes
# the check skip a draft runner. Drop the patch once the image's sgl-amd-mono has the PR.

diff --git a/sgl_amd_mono/qwen38_flash_next/draft.py b/sgl_amd_mono/qwen38_flash_next/draft.py
index 06f2783..514948b 100644
--- a/sgl_amd_mono/qwen38_flash_next/draft.py
+++ b/sgl_amd_mono/qwen38_flash_next/draft.py
@@ -20,8 +20,9 @@ the launch cannot read raises instead of running SGLang's forward; larger steps
 run SGLang's forward. ``_build`` turns SGLang's QSA MTP index sharing off for the
 draft: with it on, SGLang's draft decode reuses the selection its own draft extend
 stored, which a launched extend never writes, so a batch growing past 8 requests
-would decode with a stale selection. SGLang's capture check never sees a draft
-step, so this module logs each draft key the first time it launches. Check mode
+would decode with a stale selection. SGLang's capture check checks the target's
+steps, not a draft's (``_keep_draft_out_of_capture_check``), so this module logs each
+draft key the first time it launches. Check mode
 (``SGLANG_AMD_MONO_CHECK``) does not cover the draft yet, and fault injection arms
 the target's launches only.
 
